# [<tag>] (When this commit is applied, ...) <subject> (Maximum 72 characters)
# |<----   It is recommended to use up to 50 characters   --->|<------------------ ->|
# Example:
# [feat] Implementation of automated message logging

# (Optional) Explain why this change was made
# |<----   Try to limit each line to a maximum of 72 characters   ---->|

# (Optional) Provide links or identifiers to relevant tickets, tasks, or other resources
# Example: GitHub issue #23

# --- COMMIT END ---
# The tag can be
#    feat     (new feature)
#    fix      (bug fix)
#    refactor (code refactoring)
#    style    (formatting, missing indentation, etc.; no code changes)
#    doc      (changes to documentation)
#    test     (adding or refactoring tests; no changes to production code)
#    version  (version increment/new release; no changes to production code)
#    license  (changes related to licensing; no changes to production code)
#    hack     (workaround; please avoid this)
#    defaults (changes to default settings)
#
# --------------------
# Remember:
#   * The subject line must start with a capital letter
#   * Do not end the subject line with a period
#   * Separate the subject line from the description with a blank line
#   * Use the body to explain what, why, and how
#   * You can create lists by using “-” or “*” at the beginning of each line in the body
# --------------------
